            <ArticleTitle>Pain reduction in amputees by long-term spinal cord stimulation. Long-term follow-up study over 5 years.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>346-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This follow-up study analyzes the results of dorsal column stimulation instituted between 1972 and 1974 for the relief of pain in 84 patients, including 64 amputees. Good results decreased from 52.4% after 2 years of stimulation to 39% after 5 years. Special therapeutic problems in amputees are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
